<title>JAPAN: Japan April household spending down real 1.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan April household spending down real 1.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's household spending in April fell 1.0 percent in real terms from a year earlier to an average 343,345 yen per household, the government's Management and Coordination Agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of year-on-year percentage changes in April and March in real and nominal terms:</p>
<p>					   April		 March</p>
<p>				     Real   Nominal    Real   Nominal</p>
<p>Overall household spending   -1.0    +0.9	+5.8     +6.0</p>
<p>(average 343,345 yen)</p>
<p>Spending by wage earners     -1.1    +0.8	+6.6     +6.8</p>
<p>(average 365,983 yen)</p>
</text>
